DOC/samples -- small input files the gallery cards run on=========================================================Four files, here so that a command shown on a card is a command you canactually type.  Several programs need something to read, and a card thatsays `vi tmp/EDIT/jabber.txt' is no use on a fresh disk: /dd/tmp shipsempty.  Pointing those cards at files that ship makes the shown commandtrue as written.  jabber.txt   the first verse of `Jabberwocky', four lines.  Text to               edit, filter or count -- vi, mg, sed and sed_1.06 all use               it.  Lewis Carroll, 1871, long out of copyright.  titles       four book titles, one per line, for `pagekwic' to build a               keyword-in-context index from.  menu         three `label,command' lines, the file `mshell' reads to               draw its menu.  hello.ps     three lines of PostScript that set a font and show one               string, for `gs403' to rasterise.  cat.txt      a two-book Home Librarian catalogue in the text form               `Libr2Ascii' writes and `Ascii2Libr' reads: a page count,               a card count, two cards, then the title, author and               subject indexes.  Six cards use it -- Ascii2Libr,               Libr2Ascii, EditLibr, Librarian, PrintCards and               PrintLabels -- each turning it into a catalogue with               `Ascii2Libr -outfile tmp/cat.libr < DOC/samples/cat.txt'.               The two books are real ones and the entries are factual.  label.tpl    a three-line template for `PrintLabels': %title, %author,               %publisher, %city, %year and %id, each replaced with that               card's field once per book.The last three were written for this collection and are yours to copy,change or delete.  Nothing here is anybody's property.This is the same arrangement the disk already used elsewhere --DOC/xasm/sample.a0, DOC/logisim/counter.lsi, DOC/tex/none.ch andGAMES/rayshade/boxball.ray are all files a card runs on.